From 61ccb436837488833fb52d219c1fd83333cdc372 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Floyd <git@notmy.space>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 19:01:32 +0000
Subject: software_isp: Start the GPU debayer when the camera is configured

The EGL context, the shaders' compilation and the first frame's
texture setup ran on the first frame's request, after the sensor had
started streaming, so the first frames waited for them. Start the
debayer's worker thread, and with it the context and shaders, at the
end of configure() when the debayer can (startsAhead()), and keep the
configuration so that a configure with the same one does not restart it.
start() then only finds it started, and stop() tears it down through
stopWorker(), which also runs when the object is destroyed.

Signed-off-by: William Floyd <git@notmy.space>
---
